    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_4",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The Baltic Cup (Estonian: \"Balti turniir\" , Latvian: \"Baltijas kauss\" , Lithuanian: \"Baltijos taurė\" ) is a football competition contested between the Baltic states of Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania every two years. During the Soviet era, when all the nations were part of the Soviet Union, Belarus also took part in some of the competitions.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999927481381,
